From 48a65d4ee66ef989588e25b4521264dba8921b66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonas Karlsson <jonas.karlsson@qt.io>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 11:48:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PhysX: Pin the glibc math symbols on x86-64 only

PhysX binds expf() and powf() to their GLIBC_2.2.5 versions, so that a
library built against a newer glibc still runs on an older one. That
version is the oldest glibc of x86-64; 32-bit x86 has the same
functions as GLIBC_2.0 and no GLIBC_2.2.5 version of them at all, so
once PhysX compiles for i686 with glibc, as the Yocto core2-32 builds
do, linking anything with it fails with undefined references to
powf@GLIBC_2.2.5.

Patch 0012 already took the architectures other than the Intel family
off this path, but the Intel family still has 32-bit x86 in it. Pin the
symbols on x86-64 alone, as patch 0021, which also leaves out
emscripten, since PhysX counts it as 32-bit x86.

Amends 7533abcc02b7f9bd7953203c489ee86d55e8c909

Fixes: QTBUG-151314
Assisted-by: Claude Code
Change-Id: Iacf64ce1faf03dddc940bcd4c2b14e619601f175

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../PhysX/include/foundation/PxMath.h         |  2 +-
 ...he-glibc-math-symbols-on-x86-64-only.patch | 29 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 src/3rdparty/PhysX/patches/0021-PhysX-Pin-the-glibc-math-symbols-on-x86-64-only.patch

diff --git a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxMath.h b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxMath.h
index d7b2c4b..1b63626 100644
--- a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxMath.h
+++ b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/include/foundation/PxMath.h
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 #pragma warning(pop)
 #endif
 
-#if (PX_LINUX_FAMILY && PX_INTEL_FAMILY && !PX_EMSCRIPTEN && defined(__GLIBC__))
+#if (PX_LINUX_FAMILY && PX_X64 && defined(__GLIBC__))
 // Force linking against nothing newer than glibc v2.17 to remain compatible with platforms with older glibc versions
 __asm__(".symver expf,expf@GLIBC_2.2.5");
 __asm__(".symver powf,powf@GLIBC_2.2.5");
diff --git a/src/3rdparty/PhysX/patches/0021-PhysX-Pin-the-glibc-math-symbols-on-x86-64-only.patch b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/patches/0021-PhysX-Pin-the-glibc-math-symbols-on-x86-64-only.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c0c8185
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/3rdparty/PhysX/patches/0021-PhysX-Pin-the-glibc-math-symbols-on-x86-64-only.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+From: Jonas Karlsson <jonas.karlsson@qt.io>
+Subject: [PATCH] PhysX: Pin the glibc math symbols on x86-64 only
+
+PhysX binds expf() and powf() to their GLIBC_2.2.5 versions, so that a
+library built against a newer glibc still runs on an older one. That
+version is the oldest glibc of x86-64; 32-bit x86 has the same functions
+as GLIBC_2.0, and has no GLIBC_2.2.5 version of them at all, so every
+link on i686 with glibc fails with undefined references to
+powf@GLIBC_2.2.5. Patch 0012 already took the other architectures off
+this path; the Intel family still has 32-bit x86 in it.
+
+Pin the symbols on x86-64 alone, which also leaves out emscripten, as
+PhysX counts it as 32-bit x86.
